//
// AN OPERATOR ON A BUILT-IN TYPE IS REFUSED (`@FR-Op-Home`: "the `self` type of an `operator`
// definition is declared in the same source as the definition; on a built-in type it is
// refused"): `operator times(self: boolean, …)` would give `*` a meaning on `boolean` that no
// program declared, so it is refused at the definition.  One refusal per file.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fired as expected on 18594597b,
//   interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the built-in type.
// HOLDS: the same definition on a struct of this file compiles (Op-Name's cell).
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator times` defines `*` for a type of its own package, and `boolean` is not one

operator times(self: boolean, o: integer) -> integer { if self { o } else { 0 } }

fn main() {
  println("x");
}
